WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:03.803
-A new poll says the majority
of Americans disapprove

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:05.738
of President Trump's
handling of Iran

00:00:05.738 --> 00:00:08.308
and his own team struggles
to defend his lies

00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:10.677
and borrows directly from
George W. Bush's playbook.

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:12.645
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:14.013
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.013 --> 00:00:17.116 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:17.116 --> 00:00:19.152
-You might remember that
throughout President Obama's

00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:21.320
two terms, Republicans,
including Donald Trump,

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:23.790
objected to virtually everything
he did on the grounds

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:26.325
that he was trampling
on the Constitution

00:00:26.325 --> 00:00:27.794
they supposedly cherished.

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:30.630
-I feel very strongly about
our Constitution.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.031
I'm proud of it. I love it.

00:00:32.031 --> 00:00:34.266
And I want to go through
the Constitution.

00:00:34.266 --> 00:00:35.602
That's what we want to do.

00:00:35.602 --> 00:00:38.037
I mean, we want to bring
the Constitution back.

00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:41.807
-I will give President Obama
and the Senate Democrats credit.

00:00:41.807 --> 00:00:46.479
They believe in principles
of big government.

00:00:46.479 --> 00:00:49.515
They believe in this relentless
assault

00:00:49.515 --> 00:00:51.083
on our Constitutional rights.

00:00:51.083 --> 00:00:53.118
-This President wants to act
as if he's a king,

00:00:53.118 --> 00:00:54.587
as if he's a dictator.

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:55.855
-You see,
I think we need to return

00:00:55.855 --> 00:00:57.390
to Constitutional government.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:58.992
I think they shredded
the Constitution,

00:00:58.992 --> 00:01:00.492
especially during
the healthcare debate.

00:01:00.492 --> 00:01:03.696
-Is it time the president
just already do this already,

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:04.864
torch the Constitution?

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:07.299
-No!
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.299 --> 00:01:10.870
Not the pocket Constitution!
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:12.638
Melodrama doesn't work as well

00:01:12.638 --> 00:01:14.106
when you're threatening
a reproduction.

00:01:14.106 --> 00:01:19.512 line:0%
It's like saying, "I'm so mad,
I'm going to flip over my car!

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:21.247 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:23.949
You left me no choice."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.949 --> 00:01:25.985
Also, I wish he had actually
done it because then he'd

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:27.887
set off the fire sprinklers
at Fox News

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:29.388
and Rudy Giuliani
would have melted

00:01:29.388 --> 00:01:30.790
like the Wicked Witch
of the West.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:31.924
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.924 --> 00:01:33.993
All you would see is a suit,
some shoes,

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:37.029
and his big old Yankee ring.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.029 --> 00:01:39.699
So, the right spent eight years
constantly lecturing

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:42.401
the rest of us about the
sanctity of the Constitution

00:01:42.401 --> 00:01:43.536
and obsessively whining

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:45.438
that Obama was supposedly
shredding it.

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:47.907
And then earlier this month,
Trump ordered the strike

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:50.309
that killed a top Iranian
general, Qasem Soleimani,

00:01:50.309 --> 00:01:51.577
without Congressional approval.

00:01:51.577 --> 00:01:53.879
The Constitution clearly
and unequivocally gives Congress

00:01:53.879 --> 00:01:55.948
and only Congress the power
to declare war.

00:01:55.948 --> 00:01:58.484
And yet last week, after
the house passed a resolution

00:01:58.484 --> 00:02:00.053
reining in Trump's war powers,

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:02.822
he complained at a rally that
it would be inconvenient for him

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:06.025
to notify Congress before moving
forward with an act of war.

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:07.827
-These are split-second
decisions.

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:09.228
You have to make a decision.

00:02:09.228 --> 00:02:12.498
So they don't want me to make
that decision.

00:02:12.498 --> 00:02:15.568
They want me to call up,
maybe go over there.

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:16.903
Let me go over to Congress.

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:19.538
Come on over to the White House.
Let's talk about it.

00:02:19.538 --> 00:02:20.740
When can you make it?

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.708
Well, I won't be able
to make it today, sir.

00:02:22.708 --> 00:02:25.578
How about, uh, let's say
in a couple of days?

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:28.047
Oh, sure. Come on over.

00:02:28.047 --> 00:02:29.582
We had to make a decision.

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:32.518
We didn't have time
to call up Nancy,

00:02:32.518 --> 00:02:36.055
who is not operating
with a full deck.

00:02:36.055 --> 00:02:38.591
-She's not operating
with a full deck?

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:41.260
You're operating with
a pair of deuces

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:43.061
and that card that has
the rules on it.

00:02:43.061 --> 00:02:44.463
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:44.463 --> 00:02:49.602
So, Trump circumvented Congress

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:51.537
to launch a strike
on an official

00:02:51.537 --> 00:02:52.638
of a foreign government,

00:02:52.638 --> 00:02:54.373
a decision that has been
deeply unpopular

00:02:54.373 --> 00:02:55.474
with the American people,

00:02:55.474 --> 00:02:57.009
according to a new poll
out this week.

00:02:57.009 --> 00:02:59.779
A majority of Americans
disapprove of Trump's handling

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:01.915
of Iran and say they feel
less safe as a result.

00:03:01.915 --> 00:03:03.516
So to try to justify the attack,

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:05.284
Trump's team has claimed
that Soleimani

00:03:05.284 --> 00:03:08.220
posed an imminent threat
and that they had to stop it.

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:10.022
Although Secretary of State
Mike Pompeo

00:03:10.022 --> 00:03:12.758
has been incredibly cagey
about that.

00:03:12.758 --> 00:03:15.228
-President Trump says that
General Soleimani

00:03:15.228 --> 00:03:17.730
was planning
a "imminent attack."

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:18.998
What was the plan?

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:21.167
Who were the targets?
And how soon?

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:23.336
-There's things we simply
cannot make public about

00:03:23.336 --> 00:03:24.804
what it is we knew at that time.

00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:27.574
And what in fact we know today
about the continuing activity.

00:03:27.574 --> 00:03:29.775
-So was the justification
in that he's been

00:03:29.775 --> 00:03:32.145
this destabilizing force
in the region for so long,

00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:34.714
or was the justification
this imminent threat?

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:36.815
-Chuck, it's never one thing.

00:03:36.815 --> 00:03:39.685
-There is no doubt that were
a series of imminent attacks

00:03:39.685 --> 00:03:42.188
that were being plotted
by Qasem Soleimani.

00:03:42.188 --> 00:03:43.756
We don't know precisely when

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:45.291
and we don't know
precisely where.

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:46.392
But it was real.

00:03:46.392 --> 00:03:47.827
-When you say the attacks
were imminent,

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:49.562
how imminent were they?
Are we talking about days?

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:51.897
Are we talking about weeks?

00:03:51.897 --> 00:03:54.967
-If you're an American in
the region, days and weeks,

00:03:54.967 --> 00:03:57.070
this is not something
that's relevant.

00:03:57.070 --> 00:03:59.538
-These guys claim there's
an imminent attack,

00:03:59.538 --> 00:04:01.073
and then when you ask them
for specifics,

00:04:01.073 --> 00:04:03.543
suddenly they turn into
characters in a French film.

00:04:03.543 --> 00:04:06.879
[ French accent ] Days, weeks,
what is the difference?

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:10.182
Weeks are days,
days are weeks.

00:04:10.182 --> 00:04:12.151
What matters is love, no?

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:13.819
[ Laughter ]

00:04:13.819 --> 00:04:16.456
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:20.692 --> 00:04:22.395
Je suis Pompeo.

00:04:22.395 --> 00:04:24.263
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.263 --> 00:04:26.165
C'est vrai!

00:04:26.165 --> 00:04:27.834
Then, the Trump
administration --

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:31.971
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.971 --> 00:04:34.673
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:34.673 --> 00:04:37.376
Then, the Trump administration
sent military briefers

00:04:37.376 --> 00:04:40.746
to Congress to try to convince
them that the threat was real.

00:04:40.746 --> 00:04:43.516
But that only made things worse
with members of both parties

00:04:43.516 --> 00:04:46.752
coming away from the briefing
furious and unsatisfied.

00:04:46.752 --> 00:04:50.756
-I had hoped and expected
to receive more information

00:04:50.756 --> 00:04:52.858
outlining the legal, factual,

00:04:52.858 --> 00:04:55.261
and moral justification
for the attack.

00:04:55.261 --> 00:04:57.629
I was left somewhat unsatisfied.

00:04:57.629 --> 00:04:59.865
-There was no specific
information given to us

00:04:59.865 --> 00:05:01.199
of the specific attack.

00:05:01.199 --> 00:05:04.903
And none was overwhelming
that "X" was going to happen.

00:05:04.903 --> 00:05:07.706
-My reaction to this briefing
was it was sophomoric

00:05:07.706 --> 00:05:09.775
and utterly unconvincing.

00:05:09.775 --> 00:05:14.147
I was, well, utterly
unpersuaded

00:05:14.147 --> 00:05:17.350
about any evidence about
the imminence of a threat

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:19.819
that was new or compelling.

00:05:19.819 --> 00:05:22.822
-We did not get information
inside that briefing

00:05:22.822 --> 00:05:26.959
that there was a specific,
imminent threat.

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:29.962
I think it is likely
because it doesn't exist.

00:05:29.962 --> 00:05:31.897
-Of course it doesn't exist.

00:05:31.897 --> 00:05:34.834
If Donald Trump says,
"Trust me, the thing exists,"

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:36.502
it definitely does not exist.

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:39.172
He's like a magician who says
he's going to pull a rabbit

00:05:39.172 --> 00:05:41.007
out of his hat, looks down,

00:05:41.007 --> 00:05:42.874
realizes the rabbit
chewed through the hat

00:05:42.874 --> 00:05:44.243
and escaped, and says,

00:05:44.243 --> 00:05:45.945
[ As Trump ] Trust me,
the rabbit's there.

00:05:45.945 --> 00:05:47.146
[ Laughter ]

00:05:47.146 --> 00:05:48.447
[ Normal voice ]
So because no one believed him,

00:05:48.447 --> 00:05:50.416
Trump decided to
do his usual routine

00:05:50.416 --> 00:05:52.351
of making even more
outlandish lies,

00:05:52.351 --> 00:05:53.953
changing his story
multiple times

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:56.222
within the span
of just a few days.

00:05:56.222 --> 00:05:59.224
-We did it because they were
looking to blow up our embassy.

00:05:59.224 --> 00:06:01.094
-Mr. President?

00:06:01.094 --> 00:06:02.528
-Blow up the embassy in Baghdad?

00:06:02.528 --> 00:06:04.697
Can you provide more details
on that plot was?

00:06:04.697 --> 00:06:06.065
-No, I think it was obvious.

00:06:06.065 --> 00:06:10.236
And he had more than that
particular embassy in mind.

00:06:10.236 --> 00:06:14.307
He was looking very seriously
at our embassies,

00:06:14.307 --> 00:06:16.642
and not just the embassy
in Baghdad.

00:06:16.642 --> 00:06:18.711
-Don't the American people
have a right to know

00:06:18.711 --> 00:06:20.813
what specifically was targeted

00:06:20.813 --> 00:06:22.848
without revealing methods
and sources?

00:06:22.848 --> 00:06:24.350
-Well, I don't think so.

00:06:24.350 --> 00:06:26.552
But we will tell you
that probably

00:06:26.552 --> 00:06:29.188
it was going to be
the embassy in Baghdad.

00:06:29.188 --> 00:06:31.423
-Did he have large-scale
attacks planned

00:06:31.423 --> 00:06:33.292
for other embassies?

00:06:33.292 --> 00:06:35.895
And if those were planned,

00:06:35.895 --> 00:06:38.164
why can't we reveal that
to the American people?

00:06:38.164 --> 00:06:39.732
Wouldn't that help your case?

00:06:39.732 --> 00:06:41.133
-I can reveal that I believe

00:06:41.133 --> 00:06:42.968
it would have been
four embassies.

00:06:42.968 --> 00:06:44.971
-In the span of two days,

00:06:44.971 --> 00:06:47.340
he went from not talking
about embassies at all

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:48.807
to saying it was one embassy

00:06:48.807 --> 00:06:50.343
to saying it was
multiple embassies

00:06:50.343 --> 00:06:51.911
to saying it was four embassies.

00:06:51.911 --> 00:06:53.445
I know Trump is a bad liar,

00:06:53.445 --> 00:06:55.414
but even for him it's obvious
he's making stuff up

00:06:55.414 --> 00:06:56.716
off the top of his head.

00:06:56.716 --> 00:06:58.250
[ As Trump ]
What if it was four embassies?

00:06:58.250 --> 00:07:01.087
Is that a number where you
would all leave me alone?

00:07:01.087 --> 00:07:02.721
[ Laughter ]

00:07:02.721 --> 00:07:04.924
What if they were
Embassy Suites?

00:07:04.924 --> 00:07:07.827
I mean that --
That would be bad, right?

00:07:07.827 --> 00:07:11.397
That would be a bad thing.
[ Applause ]

00:07:11.397 --> 00:07:13.566
[ Normal voice ] In fact,
Trump's lies have spun

00:07:13.566 --> 00:07:16.635
so far out of control that even
his own defense secretary,

00:07:16.635 --> 00:07:19.905
Mark Esper, had a hard time
defending him this weekend

00:07:19.905 --> 00:07:21.907
when he made the rounds
on the Sunday shows.

00:07:21.907 --> 00:07:24.677
-Many members of Congress,
from both parties,

00:07:24.677 --> 00:07:27.179
have said that none
of the briefings

00:07:27.179 --> 00:07:29.882
mentioned threats
to four U.S. embassies.

00:07:29.882 --> 00:07:33.018
Why is president Trump
telling this to Fox News,

00:07:33.018 --> 00:07:35.788
but the administration is not
briefing Congress

00:07:35.788 --> 00:07:37.223
on this threat
of four embassies

00:07:37.223 --> 00:07:40.459
unless there was actually
no specific intelligence

00:07:40.459 --> 00:07:42.094
that there was a threat
to four embassies?

00:07:42.094 --> 00:07:44.496
The president never said there
was specific intelligence.

00:07:44.496 --> 00:07:46.832
What the president said was
he believed

00:07:46.832 --> 00:07:48.634
that there probably and could
have been attacks

00:07:48.634 --> 00:07:49.902
against additional embassies.

00:07:49.902 --> 00:07:51.971
The president didn't say there
was a tangible --

00:07:51.971 --> 00:07:53.772
He didn't state a specific
piece of evidence.

00:07:53.772 --> 00:07:54.740
What he said is he probably --

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:55.874
he believed it could have
been --

00:07:55.874 --> 00:07:57.476
-Are you saying there
wasn't one?

00:07:57.476 --> 00:07:59.678
-I didn't see one with regard
to four embassies.

00:07:59.678 --> 00:08:01.146
-You're the
Secretary of Defense.

00:08:01.146 --> 00:08:04.050
If it's real,
why wouldn't you have seen it?

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:06.586
You think Donald Trump has
his own top secret intelligence

00:08:06.586 --> 00:08:07.753
he's not sharing with anyone

00:08:07.753 --> 00:08:09.455
until he blurts it out
on Fox News?

00:08:09.455 --> 00:08:11.190
You think he's out there
parachuting

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:13.292
into the Iraqi desert with
night vision goggles...

00:08:13.292 --> 00:08:15.194
[ Laughter ]
...collecting intel on his own.

00:08:15.194 --> 00:08:17.563
[ As Trump ] Bad news, guys.
Everything's green.

00:08:17.563 --> 00:08:19.064
[ Laughter ]

00:08:19.064 --> 00:08:22.101
[ Normal voice ] Now if you're
getting a feeling of déjà vu

00:08:22.101 --> 00:08:24.169
at this point, it's because
we've been through this before

00:08:24.169 --> 00:08:26.972
in the run-up to the Iraq war
in 2002 and 2003.

00:08:26.972 --> 00:08:28.874
The Bush administration
repeatedly lied

00:08:28.874 --> 00:08:31.310
about the intelligence they used
to justify that war

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:32.712
in eerily similar ways.

00:08:32.712 --> 00:08:34.946
They claimed definitively
that Saddam Hussein

00:08:34.946 --> 00:08:36.582
had weapons of mass destruction

00:08:36.582 --> 00:08:38.550
and that he had ties to
the terrorists

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:40.119
who carried out 9/11.

00:08:40.119 --> 00:08:41.787
They manipulated intelligence

00:08:41.787 --> 00:08:44.190
and concocted all kinds of lies
about that intelligence

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:46.525
to justify an immoral
and catastrophic war

00:08:46.525 --> 00:08:48.494
that destabilized the region
and the world.

00:08:48.494 --> 00:08:50.796
And they were adamant
and unequivocal about it.

00:08:50.796 --> 00:08:52.964
Of course,
in George W. Bush's case,

00:08:52.964 --> 00:08:55.100
he couldn't always keep
his talking points straight.

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:57.436
-There is no doubt
that Saddam Hussein

00:08:57.436 --> 00:08:59.805
now has weapons
of mass destruction.

00:08:59.805 --> 00:09:02.241
There is no doubt that
he is amassing them

00:09:02.241 --> 00:09:03.876
to use against our friends,

00:09:03.876 --> 00:09:06.411
against our allies,
and against us.

00:09:06.411 --> 00:09:08.547
-No terrorist state poses

00:09:08.547 --> 00:09:11.150
a greater or more immediate
threat to the security

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:12.918
of our people and the stability
of the world

00:09:12.918 --> 00:09:16.121
than the regime
of Saddam Hussein in Iraq.

00:09:16.121 --> 00:09:20.225
-There's a lot of talk about
Iraq on our TV screens.

00:09:20.225 --> 00:09:21.994
And there should be.

00:09:21.994 --> 00:09:23.395
Because we're trying
to figure out

00:09:23.395 --> 00:09:27.700
how best to make the world
a peaceful place.

00:09:27.700 --> 00:09:29.902
There's an old saying
in Tennessee,

00:09:29.902 --> 00:09:31.504
I know it's in Texas,
probably in Tennessee,

00:09:31.504 --> 00:09:36.809
that says fool me once,
shame on...

00:09:36.809 --> 00:09:41.647
shame on you.

00:09:41.647 --> 00:09:43.115
Fool me --
you can't get fooled again.

00:09:43.115 --> 00:09:45.217
[ Laughter ]

00:09:45.217 --> 00:09:48.654
-Is that -- that's how
they say it in Texas?

00:09:48.654 --> 00:09:49.922
[ Laughter ]

00:09:49.922 --> 00:09:51.490
[ As Bush ] There's
an old saying in Texas,

00:09:51.490 --> 00:09:54.893
give a man a fish, and now...

00:09:54.893 --> 00:09:56.662
that man has a fish.

00:09:56.662 --> 00:09:58.230
[ Laughter ]

00:09:58.230 --> 00:10:00.899
And he can eat that fish.

00:10:00.899 --> 00:10:04.403
Or he can keep it as a pet.
What I'm saying is...

00:10:04.403 --> 00:10:08.807
Saddam Hussein is stockpiling
weapons of bass destruction.

00:10:08.807 --> 00:10:10.308
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:10.308 --> 00:10:12.778
[ Normal voice ] Remember when
we thought we could never elect

00:10:12.778 --> 00:10:14.480
a dumber President
than George W. Bush?

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:17.215
And then, yesterday,
our current president

00:10:17.215 --> 00:10:20.319
tweeted about impeachment
and said, "Hose Republicans...

00:10:20.319 --> 00:10:22.188
[ Laughter ]

00:10:22.188 --> 00:10:24.690
...voted 195-0 against it."

00:10:24.690 --> 00:10:27.960
Well, I mean, I guess we can't
expect the real-estate developer

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:29.662
to be able to spell the word
"house."

00:10:29.662 --> 00:10:31.830
[ Laughter ]

00:10:31.830 --> 00:10:35.334
Also, he lives in the most
famous house in the world.

00:10:35.334 --> 00:10:37.636
And because none of his aides
will ever tell him he's wrong,

00:10:37.636 --> 00:10:39.972
they're gonna have to change
all of the signs now.

00:10:39.972 --> 00:10:42.207
[ Laughter ]

00:10:42.207 --> 00:10:43.709
And then at his rally
last week,

00:10:43.709 --> 00:10:45.811
Trump could barely get through
the standard end

00:10:45.811 --> 00:10:48.413
of his stump speech without
sounding like he just downed

00:10:48.413 --> 00:10:49.749
a bottle of Novocain.

00:10:49.749 --> 00:10:53.318
-We will make America
wealthy again.

00:10:53.318 --> 00:10:57.389
We will make America
srrong again.

00:10:57.389 --> 00:10:58.491
[ Laughter ]

00:10:58.491 --> 00:11:00.926
-Did he just do a keg stand?

00:11:00.926 --> 00:11:04.062
If your friend started
talking like that,

00:11:04.062 --> 00:11:07.432
you'd rush them to the hospital
to have their stomach pumped.

00:11:07.432 --> 00:11:09.602
He sounds like he just got
knocked out in the first round

00:11:09.602 --> 00:11:10.569
by Ronda Rousey.

00:11:10.569 --> 00:11:11.603
"Donald, don't get up."

00:11:11.603 --> 00:11:12.871
[ As Trump, slurring ]
I can do it.

00:11:12.871 --> 00:11:15.341
I'm feeling srrong again.

00:11:15.341 --> 00:11:16.942
[ Laughter ]

00:11:16.942 --> 00:11:19.778
[ Normal voice ] And I think
even Trump knows on some level

00:11:19.778 --> 00:11:22.281
that he can't paper over
his lies with charm

00:11:22.281 --> 00:11:23.481
because he doesn't have any.

00:11:23.481 --> 00:11:25.384
In fact,
he seemed to admit as much

00:11:25.384 --> 00:11:27.386
in this brief flash
of self-awareness

00:11:27.386 --> 00:11:28.687
at his rally last week.

00:11:28.687 --> 00:11:33.425
-The radical Democrats
have never been more extreme

00:11:33.425 --> 00:11:34.893
than they are right now.

00:11:34.893 --> 00:11:37.896
They are stone-cold crazy.

00:11:37.896 --> 00:11:41.366
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:41.366 --> 00:11:44.236
You know, it's interesting,
as I'm saying this stuff,

00:11:44.236 --> 00:11:46.672
you know, they want crime,
they want chaos.

00:11:46.672 --> 00:11:48.440
I'm saying all this stuff.
And then I say,

00:11:48.440 --> 00:11:51.744
"Geez, now I sort of understand
why they hate me." Right?

00:11:51.744 --> 00:11:56.182
-Wow. It's like he just had
a breakthrough in therapy.

00:11:56.182 --> 00:11:57.949
[ Laughter ]

00:11:57.949 --> 00:12:01.086
He should had a psychiatrist
on stage next to him saying,

00:12:01.086 --> 00:12:04.156
"Expand on that."
[ Laughter ]

00:12:04.156 --> 00:12:07.325
Anyway, the point is
the Bush administration

00:12:07.325 --> 00:12:08.994
manipulated an intelligence lie

00:12:08.994 --> 00:12:11.697
and insisted that Saddam Hussein
had weapons of mass destruction

00:12:11.697 --> 00:12:13.698
and ties to the terrorists
who carried out 9/11.

00:12:13.698 --> 00:12:16.368
And as just as we've seen with
Trump, Pompeo, and Esper,

00:12:16.368 --> 00:12:18.938
even when Bush officials
admitted there was uncertainty

00:12:18.938 --> 00:12:20.739
and disagreement about
the intelligence,

00:12:20.739 --> 00:12:22.841
they used ominous language
to cow people

00:12:22.841 --> 00:12:25.010
who dared to question them
into backing down.

00:12:25.010 --> 00:12:27.245
-You will get different
estimates about

00:12:27.245 --> 00:12:28.981
precisely how close he is.

00:12:28.981 --> 00:12:31.950
We do know that he is actively

00:12:31.950 --> 00:12:35.020
pursuing a nuclear weapon.

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:38.290
There will always be some
uncertainty

00:12:38.290 --> 00:12:41.360
about how quickly he can
acquire a nuclear weapon.

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:44.229
But we don't want the smoking
gun to be a mushroom cloud.

00:12:44.229 --> 00:12:48.901
-We cannot wait for the final
proof, the smoking gun,

00:12:48.901 --> 00:12:51.770
that could come in the form
of a mushroom cloud.

00:12:51.770 --> 00:12:53.004
-Remember that line?

00:12:53.004 --> 00:12:55.140
So many of the most powerful
people

00:12:55.140 --> 00:12:56.575
in our most powerful
institutions

00:12:56.575 --> 00:12:59.044
went along with that line,
though it was obviously insane.

00:12:59.044 --> 00:13:01.413
It's like if your husband said,
"I think I have a UTI."

00:13:01.413 --> 00:13:02.747
And you were like,
"No, you don't."

00:13:02.747 --> 00:13:05.116
And he was like, "Okay.
Well, I guess we'll find out

00:13:05.116 --> 00:13:07.019
when my penis falls off!"

00:13:07.019 --> 00:13:11.223
[ Laughter ]

00:13:11.223 --> 00:13:12.691
Of course it turns out
there was neither

00:13:12.691 --> 00:13:14.326
a mushroom cloud
nor a smoking gun,

00:13:14.326 --> 00:13:16.695
or as Trump has repeatedly
called it, "a smocking gun."

00:13:16.695 --> 00:13:19.598
That's probably why Trump's
speech writers

00:13:19.598 --> 00:13:21.934
have never even bothered to
write a line like that for him

00:13:21.934 --> 00:13:24.069
because they know he'd never
be able to pronounce the words.

00:13:24.069 --> 00:13:26.004
[ As Trump ] We know don't
want the smocking gun

00:13:26.004 --> 00:13:28.574
to be a mushroom pizza.

00:13:28.574 --> 00:13:30.108
[ Laughter ]

00:13:30.108 --> 00:13:32.578
That is something
that cannot be...

00:13:32.578 --> 00:13:33.978
-Tolerited.

00:13:33.978 --> 00:13:35.981
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:13:35.981 --> 00:13:37.949
-[ Normal voice ] We've been
through this before --

00:13:37.949 --> 00:13:39.885
a lawless administration

00:13:39.885 --> 00:13:42.120
lying to justify
a potentially disastrous

00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:43.322
and illegal act of war.

00:13:43.322 --> 00:13:45.257
Trump pulled back from the brink
last week,

00:13:45.257 --> 00:13:47.258
but it's very possible he could
do this all over again,

00:13:47.258 --> 00:13:50.061
which means Congress must use
its power to stop him.

00:13:50.061 --> 00:13:51.797
Because as they say in Texas...

00:13:51.797 --> 00:13:53.431
-You can't get fooled again.

00:13:53.431 --> 00:13:55.601
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:13:55.601 --> 00:13:57.002
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:13:57.002 --> 00:13:59.271 line:0%
♪♪

